  "body": "Yes. This is a strong Kibbitzing setup because the scene can make the disagreement feel affectionate and socially playful rather than hostile.\n\nIf you're looking to turn this into the actual video prompt, I’d tighten it slightly so the model emphasizes the Klingon taking the conversation extremely seriously while FOUND is calmly kibbitzing back at him:\n\nVideo Prompt 1: The Klingon Disagreement in the Park\n\nA cinematic, photorealistic 8K medium shot of FOUND sitting cross-legged on a lush green grass bank beside a quiet Amsterdam canal at dusk. The setting is unmistakably Dutch but subtle and natural: calm canal water, historic brick apartment buildings, soft evening light, and a peaceful public park atmosphere.\n\nTwo white geese rest nearby on the grass. They occasionally tilt their heads toward FOUND but remain completely unbothered.\n\nFOUND wears her signature black tactical suit. Her dark hair is pulled into a high bun. Her matte-black face mask carries a small glowing neon-white FOUND badge.\n\nIn her hand, she holds a translucent futuristic smartphone projecting a realistic holographic video call. On the holographic display is her elderly Klingon warrior mentor: an imposing, battle-worn Klingon with a deeply ridged forehead, grey beard, traditional Klingon armor, and an intensely stern expression.\n\nThe Klingon mentor is clearly in the middle of a passionate disagreement. He gestures emphatically and growls with the absolute authority of a legendary warrior giving crucial battlefield instructions.\n\nFOUND listens patiently.\n\nShe then slowly shakes her head.\n\nA small pause.\n\nShe looks directly at the holographic Klingon, completely calm, and firmly replies:\n\n“Qo’!”\n\nHer delivery is decisive but not angry. It feels like she has had this argument with him many times before.\n\nThe Klingon becomes even more animated.\n\nFOUND simply raises one hand in a calm “no” gesture, as though patiently kibbitzing with an overly dramatic old friend.\n\nThe contrast is humorous: an ancient Klingon warrior conducting an extremely serious argument while his apprentice sits peacefully beside an Amsterdam canal with two completely indifferent geese.\n\nThe geese briefly look at each other, then return to resting.\n\nThe camera makes a slow, elegant orbital movement around FOUND, keeping her and the holographic Klingon in focus while gradually revealing the tranquil Dutch surroundings.\n\nThe mood is cinematic, affectionate, slightly absurd, and deadpan rather than comedic slapstick.\n\nNatural dusk lighting, subtle reflections on the canal, realistic skin and fabric textures, detailed Klingon armor, believable holographic light interaction, shallow depth of field, cinematic composition, 24fps film look, subtle film grain, photorealistic lighting, restrained cinematic color grading.\n\nImportant: The Klingon should feel genuinely intimidating and authoritative. FOUND should remain completely composed. The humor comes from the contrast, not exaggerated acting.The “kibbitzing” layer is particularly good here: FOUND isn't fighting her mentor. She's essentially sitting in a Dutch park having a very serious “No, you're wrong, old man” conversation with a Klingon. 😄",
